# Stage 1 — Extract & Analyze

## Key Findings from Documents

**System scope:** A production-grade multi-agent system combining LangGraph (workflow orchestration) + CrewAI (collaborative agent teams) + Ollama (local LLM serving), with a full-duplex voice interface and HITL gates.

**Deliverables identified (grouped):**

| Category | Components |
|---|---|
| **Root artifacts** | `.env`, `README.md`, `requirements.txt`, `main.py` |
| **Configuration** | 4 YAML files (agents, tasks, llm_config, system_settings) |
| **Data models** | 3 Pydantic schemas + `AgentState` (TypedDict) |
| **Custom tools** | 5 tools (GitHub, Kaggle, web_search, document_parser, Ollama) |
| **Services** | STT, TTS, audio_stream_handler, db_manager, S3 manager |
| **Utilities** | data_preprocessing, llm_client, error_handling |
| **CrewAI crews** | 6 crews (Profile, SkillGap, LearningPath, Project, FineTuning, ProgressReporting) |
| **LangGraph nodes** | 7 nodes + graph.py + state.py |
| **Tests** | Unit (nodes, agents, tools) + Integration (full workflow) |
| **Infra/Scripts** | `setup_ollama.sh`, `deploy.sh`, docker-compose |
| **Observability** | LangSmith tracing, Prometheus metrics, structlog |
| **Docs/Notebooks** | architecture_document.md, fine-tuning experiment notebook |

**Hard constraints discovered:**
- `project_generation` + `llm_fine_tuning` must run in parallel (asyncio.gather) → both depend on `learning_path` and both block `progress_report`.
- HITL gate uses LangGraph `interrupt()` — needs checkpoint persistence (Redis/Postgres) to be operational first.
- LLM routing requires two Ollama models pulled (`llama3.2:3b` and `llama3.1:70b`) — large model pull is bandwidth-sensitive.
- Retry policy: ×3 exponential backoff on tool/crew errors; ValidationError triggers re-prompt — this must be wired into the error_handling module before crews are integration-tested.

**Assumptions made (not explicit in docs):**
1. Team of 3–5 engineers (backend, ML, voice/infra).
2. Kickoff Monday **2026-06-01**; 5-day work week.
3. Foundation work (env, Ollama, Docker, models, configs) is fully prerequisite before crew work begins.
4. Crew development can start in parallel once tools + LLM client are stable.
5. LangGraph nodes are largely thin wrappers around crews, so node work begins when its corresponding crew is ~70% complete.
6. Voice interface (STT/TTS/audio stream) is developed in parallel with crews because it touches no crew internals.
7. UAT/HITL hardening rolls into the integration phase.

**Missing info inferred:**
- No explicit release date → set as **2026-10-02** (≈ 18 weeks).
- No team allocation table → resources assigned by role below.
- No mention of CI/CD pipeline → folded into Deployment phase.

